    "body": "A useful implementation constraint is that this probably shouldn't mean N sequential chooser round trips.\n\nFor coordinated-device applications, the latency/UX win comes from one chooser transaction that returns a set of permissions. A testable acceptance criterion could be: selecting N devices requires one user activation and one chooser session, then all N appear in `getDevices()`.\n\nThat also makes cancellation semantics clear: cancelling the chooser grants none of the newly selected devices.\n",
